; Does branch 1's doubled write land at the TEMPLATE path or deeper?
; With a fully-ground template the doubled path "(ok" "3" "(ok)" still PRINTS as
; (ok), so the dump cannot tell.  Removing (ok) can: (- (ok)) subtracts a value at
; depth 3, which cannot touch a value sitting at depth 9.
; upstream expected: (ok) SURVIVES the removal and (still) is emitted
;                    => the branch-1 write really is root-prefixed (depth 9).
(f a)
(f b)
(f c)
(exec 0 (, (f $x)) (O (count (ok) 3 $x)))
(exec 1 (, (f a)) (O (- (ok))))
(exec 2 (, (ok)) (, (still)))
